# Secrets — .env and ANY backup variant (.env.bak-*, etc.) must never be visible to git
# (public repo). .env.example is tracked and intentionally NOT matched by these patterns.
.env
.env.bak*
.env.*.bak

# Python / venv
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Session + transcript logs
logs/

# Inter-agent coordination drops (ephemeral message-passing with the gabagent brain, joined on
# session_id — not project source; kept on disk locally but never tracked).
GABAGENT_*.md
VOICE_MODE_*.md

# uv
# (uv.lock IS committed for reproducibility — do not ignore it)

# Local Pipecat fork (escape hatch — see pyproject.toml [tool.uv.sources])
vendor/

# Wake-word training (isolated venv + multi-GB datasets/clips/features — never tracked).
# Keep the tooling + docs (config.yaml, *.sh, RUN*.md); IGNORE all audio/data/logs. The captured
# clips (voice_pos/, aec_neg/, selfneg/, raw_*.wav) contain the user's REAL VOICE — never push to the
# public repo (same reason as wakewords/aria_nano*.onnx below).
train-env/
wake-train/data/
wake-train/features/
wake-train/trained_models/
wake-train/music/
wake-train/voice_pos/
wake-train/aec_neg/
wake-train/selfneg/
wake-train/voiceid/
wake-train/SonicWeave-v2/
wake-train/SonicWeave-v2.zip
wake-train/NwwResourcesModel/
wake-train/*.wav
wake-train/*.log

# Model caches downloaded on first run (Whisper / Kokoro / Silero / SmartTurn)
models/
*.onnx
*.bin
# ...but DO version our own small, self-trained wake-word models (e.g. hey_aria.onnx).
!wakewords/*.onnx
# ...EXCEPT speaker-specific voice models (trained on a real user's voice) — keep those local.
# Train your own per wake-train/RUN.md; the bare openWakeWord aria.onnx ships as a starting point.
wakewords/aria_nano*.onnx

# AUR packaging build artifacts (the PKGBUILD/.SRCINFO/.install ARE tracked; build output is not)
aur/src/
aur/pkg/
aur/*.pkg.tar.zst
aur/*.log
aur/voice-agent-git/

# Local-only working directories — never shipped:
#   comms/         inter-agent coordination notes (superset of the GABAGENT_*/VOICE_MODE_* globs above —
#                  ignore the whole dir so a stray non-matching note can't slip in)
#   wake-train/    real-voice wake-word training scratchpad (multi-GB; the granular rules above already
#                  drop the voice data — this blanket is belt-and-suspenders; the shipped training doc is
#                  wakewords/README.md)
#   docs/research/ in-progress research drafts (promoted into PLAN/docs when finalized)
comms/
wake-train/
docs/research/

# Local-only scratch + hardware artifacts (never shipped):
#   scratchpad/  session working docs (folded into memory when finalized)
#   hardware/    local CAD / 3D-print sources (e.g. mega4-case OpenSCAD) — kept on disk, not tracked
#   result.json  OrcaSlicer slice-export byproduct
scratchpad/
hardware/
result.json
